                        "content": "A client has a prescription to take guaifenesin. The nurse determines that the client understands the proper administration of this medication if the client states they will perform which action?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "a0f7d178f7b728b8bba7ef20ddeca62d",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Evaluating 评价",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nGuaifenesin is an expectorant and needs to be taken with a full glass of water to decrease the viscosity of secretions. Extra doses would not be taken. The client would contact the primary health care provider if the cough lasts longer than 1 week or is accompanied by fever, rash, sore throat, or persistent headache. Fluids are needed to decrease the viscosity of secretions. The medication does not have to be taken with meals.",
                        "id": "2212513532014dc1a9bfd07f394db5c8",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "2c7cd15401c54952b5d59db7ba8b71d7",
                                "content": "Nausea and vomiting"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "209da7a2e604473fa1cc60456c7effa9",
                                "content": "Headache and level of consciousness"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "cd94f10c110247a1a99e7346377f0046",
                                "content": "Lung sounds and presence of dyspnea"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "7ea39fa0a34349fe8759a00f30c4dc8e",
                                "content": "Urine output and blood urea nitrogen level"
                            }
                        ],
